<Page
  title="About Us"
  heading="About Em Dash Remover"
  description="Why we built a free, privacy-first, grammar-aware em dash remover and AI text cleaner."
>
  <p>
    <strong>Em Dash Remover</strong> is a free tool that cleans the tell-tale signs of
    AI-generated writing out of your text - em dashes (-), curly quotes, invisible
    "watermark" characters, leftover markdown, and the clichéd phrasing that makes
    writing read like a chatbot.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we built it</h2>
  <p>
    AI writing assistants are everywhere, and they leave fingerprints. The most
    famous is the em dash: models reach for it far more than most human writers do.
    Existing tools mostly do a blind find-and-replace - turning every em dash into a
    comma - which quietly breaks your grammar and creates comma splices.
  </p>
  <p>
    We thought writers deserved better. So we built an engine that looks at the
    sentence around each em dash and chooses the <em>right</em> fix - a comma,
    semicolon, colon, period, or parentheses - so your writing stays correct, not
    just dash-free.
  </p>

  <h2>Our principles</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Privacy first.</strong> Everything runs inside your browser. Your text is never uploaded, stored, or logged. The tool even works offline.</li>
    <li><strong>Quality, not deception.</strong> We help you write more clearly and naturally - we are not a tool for cheating or "beating" AI detectors.</li>
    <li><strong>Free and open.</strong> No signup, no limits, no paywall on the core tool.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What it cleans</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Em dashes and en dashes (with smart, grammar-aware replacement)</li>
    <li>Curly "smart" quotes and apostrophes</li>
    <li>Ellipsis characters and non-breaking spaces</li>
    <li>Invisible / zero-width / watermark characters</li>
    <li>Leftover markdown formatting</li>
    <li>An AI-tell score that flags clichéd phrases and overused vocabulary</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Have an idea or found a bug? We'd love to hear from you - visit our
    <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</Page>
